From 5cb3eb22da64e0ae9895a2270e91dae9c0c0cced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor <viktor@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:57:18 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: Vulkan/Eevee shadow flicker backports for 5.2.3

Backport of the upstream fixes that are candidates for the reported
flickering/black surfaces in EEVEE with the Vulkan backend while moving
the camera:

- 05caad5ac73 Fix: Vulkan: Missing layout transitions of layered attachments
  add_image_barrier() merged barriers by image handle only, so only the
  first subresource (layer/mip) of a layered attachment (e.g. the shadow
  atlas) was transitioned back out of the rendering layout, leaving the
  other layers with stale contents.

- c394b602b67 EEVEE: Shadow: Clear rendermap to invalid pages
  The render map was only partially written each update; entries for
  tiles that are not rendered kept garbage page indices, which the
  surface shadow shader sampled.

- 14ea6ab71f7 EEVEE: Shadow: Speedup render by not tagging usage for each
  update loop (only reset SHADOW_IS_USED once per render loop).

All three applied without conflicts.
